{
  "summary": "Fixes `bitcoin-wallet create` to return an error status code when wallet creation fails. Previously, `ExecuteWalletToolFunc` fell through and returned `true` even if `MakeWallet` returned null, causing the tool to exit with status 0. The PR makes the `create` command return `false` on failure and adds a regression test case in `tool_wallet.py`.",
  "problem": "Running `bitcoin-wallet create` exits with status 0 even when wallet creation fails (for instance, when the destination wallet database already exists). Scripts and external automation checking process exit codes cannot detect that wallet creation failed.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description demonstrates that attempting to create a wallet at an existing path prints 'Database already exists.' but returns exit code 0 (`$? == 0`).",
    "PR description notes inconsistency with other tool commands: 'The other commands (info, dump, createfromdump) all return false on failure. So scripts that check the exit code think the wallet was created.'"
  ],
